\title{ggstatsplot: 'ggplot2' Based Plots with Statistical Details}
\description{
\code{{ggstatsplot}} is an extension of \code{{ggplot2}} that creates graphics with
details from statistical tests included in the plots themselves. It provides
an easier API to generate information-rich plots for statistical analysis of
continuous (box/violin plots, scatterplots, histograms, dot plots,
dot-and-whisker plots) or categorical (pie and bar charts) data. It supports
the most common types of statistical tests: parametric, nonparametric,
robust, and Bayesian versions of \emph{t}-test/ANOVA, correlation analyses,
contingency table analysis, meta-analysis, and regression analyses.
}
\details{
The main functions are:
\itemize{
\item \code{\link[=ggbetweenstats]{ggbetweenstats()}}: box/violin plots for comparisons \emph{between} groups
or conditions.
\item \code{\link[=ggwithinstats]{ggwithinstats()}}: box/violin plots for comparisons \emph{within} groups or
conditions (repeated measures).
\item \code{\link[=ggscatterstats]{ggscatterstats()}}: scatterplots with marginal distributions from
\code{{ggside}}.
\item \code{\link[=ggpiestats]{ggpiestats()}} and \code{\link[=ggbarstats]{ggbarstats()}}: pie charts and stacked bar charts
for categorical data.
\item \code{\link[=gghistostats]{gghistostats()}}: histograms for a single numeric variable, with
results from a one-sample test.
\item \code{\link[=ggdotplotstats]{ggdotplotstats()}}: Cleveland-style dot plots for labeled numeric data,
with results from a one-sample test.
\item \code{\link[=ggcorrmat]{ggcorrmat()}}: correlation matrices.
\item \code{\link[=ggcoefstats]{ggcoefstats()}}: dot-and-whisker plots for regression analyses.
}

All of them except \code{ggcoefstats()} have \code{grouped_} variants that repeat the
analysis across the levels of a grouping variable and combine the plots with
\code{\link[=combine_plots]{combine_plots()}}.

References: Patil (2021) \doi{10.21105/joss.03167}.

For more documentation, see the dedicated
\href{https://www.indrapatil.com/ggstatsplot/}{Website}.
